<%#  Modals section of the living style guide (admin/style).

     The REAL Turf Monster modal system, ported into the engine and made
     live-openable. A page-scoped host (dsModals) mirrors the shared host's full
     API — open / swap / advance / close / current + the enter-animation
     registry — so every specimen opens the genuine full-size modal built from
     the engine partials, without colliding with the app-level shared host that
     application.html.erb already mounts on $store.modals.

     Why page-scoped (dsModals) and not $store.modals: both MS and TM render the
     shared studio/modals/host once at layout level with an unconditional x-if on
     $store.modals.current(), registering ONLY that app's own modal ids. Pushing
     a novel specimen id onto $store.modals would make that host paint an empty
     card behind ours. So this section owns a tiny, self-contained store + overlay
     and registers all specimen content itself.

     Groups: Auth (the sign-in step machine), Eligibility and entry (the
     app-supplied-policy age-gate DOB primitive, gated by Studio.feature?(:age_gate),
     plus the app-specific entry-tokens purchase flow documented via engine chrome),
     Profile (crop / upload, opened
     through studio/cropper_assets), Web3 (wallet-connect with engine-owned inline
     brand icons / on-chain-tx / deposit / the generic entry-confirmed celebration,
     gated by Studio.feature?(:web3) — disabled-but-present-yet-openable when off),
     System and status (the reusable card blocks), Templates (the copy-from
     archetypes), and Rewards (level-up + the entry-confirmed seeds bar + the
     Free Entry Earned reward, gated by :leveling).

     The modal motion (modal-card-* / modal-backdrop-* keyframes + studio-modal-
     drain + body.modal-open) ships in engine-motion.css, so a consumer that
     bundles it animates these for real. %>
<%
  web3_on     = Studio.feature?(:web3)
  leveling_on = Studio.feature?(:leveling)
  age_gate_on = Studio.feature?(:age_gate)

  # Auth method-toggle defaults — mirror the app's Studio.auth_method? config;
  # Solana Wallet also needs the web3 capability, so it defaults OFF on an app
  # (like McRitchie Studio) that ships web3 off.
  ml_default = Studio.auth_method?(:magic_link)
  g_default  = Studio.auth_method?(:google)
  w_default  = Studio.auth_method?(:wallet) && web3_on

  # Active-card glow-match expression builder: yields an Alpine boolean that is
  # true when $store.dsModals.current() is THIS specimen's modal. It discriminates
  # by sub-state so specimens that open the SAME modal id still glow the right
  # card, and so the glow FOLLOWS a walked flow as the step machine advances:
  #   step:         the auth / entry-tokens step machine (step_default is the
  #                 modal's own default step — 'credentials' for auth, 'picker'
  #                 for entry-tokens).
  #   state:        the on-chain-tx state (processing / success / error) — lets the
  #                 glow track Connect Wallet -> Processing -> On-chain success.
  #   crop:         the two crop-photo variants (:picker vs :crop), on props.cropReady.
  #   celebrate:    the input specimen (form) vs the "updated" (celebrate) specimen
  #                 of the SAME leveling modal id.
  ds_glow = lambda do |id, step: nil, step_default: "credentials", crop: nil, celebrate: nil, state: nil|
    cur  = "$store.dsModals.current()"
    expr = "#{cur} && #{cur}.id === '#{id}'"
    expr += " && (#{cur}.props.step || '#{step_default}') === '#{step}'" if step
    expr += " && #{cur}.props.state === '#{state}'" if state
    expr += (crop == :crop ? " && !!#{cur}.props.cropReady" : " && !#{cur}.props.cropReady") unless crop.nil?
    expr += (celebrate ? " && !!#{cur}.props.celebrate" : " && !#{cur}.props.celebrate") unless celebrate.nil?
    expr
  end
%>
<%# DEMO flow wiring (style-page only): the age-gate primitive fires an
    'age-verified' window event on a successful confirm — its designed handoff
    hook, the same one a production app listens for to resume the entry. Here the
    style page plays that "app": on age-verified it opens the entry-token purchase
    modal, so the DS walks eligibility to purchase in sequence. The engine
    primitive is untouched; its real submit still posts to the app-supplied
    submit_url. Kept on the section (always mounted) so it fires even as the
    age-gate card closes. %>
<section id="modals" class="space-y-10" style="scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-h, 0px) + 5rem)"
         x-data="{}" @ds-modal-close.window="$store.dsModals.close()"
         @age-verified.window="$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'picker' })">
  <div class="space-y-1">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Modals</h2>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm">
      The shared modal host and the reusable modal partials, ported from Turf
      Monster into the engine. Each tile is a <strong>visual representation, not
      to scale</strong> &mdash; <strong>click a whole card</strong> to open the real
      modal (Enter/Space work too). The header <strong>Copy</strong> yields an
      agent-ready reference you can paste into a chat; option <strong>toggles</strong>
      configure the modal before you open it; and the card that matches the open
      modal + step <strong>glows</strong>, following the step machine as it advances.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# ---- Page-scoped modal host (dsModals) --------------------------------
      The full store API — open(id, props, opts) LIFO stack, swap() directional
      slide, advance(patch, opts) in-modal step change, close / closeAll,
      current(), cardClasses() driving the enter/exit animation registry, and
      body.modal-open scroll lock. Plus the dsSolanaModal proxy over the store
      (stable show/success/error/close API for the on-chain-tx modal) and the
      credential stubs (postMagicLink / walletProvider / solanaWalletConnect) so
      the auth + wallet specimens run without an auth backend. Defined in a plain
      inline script (no importmap dependency) so Alpine's defer finds it. %>
  <script>
    (function () {
      // === Credential stubs — never clobber a real one an app already ships. ==
      window.postMagicLink = window.postMagicLink || function () {
        return Promise.resolve({ success: true });
      };
      window.solanaWalletConnect = window.solanaWalletConnect || function () {
        return { connecting: false, error: null, statusText: 'Connect Wallet',
                 walletAvailable: false, isMobile: false, connect: function () {} };
      };
      window.walletProvider = window.walletProvider || {
        available: function () { return [{ name: 'Phantom' }, { name: 'Solflare' }]; },
        isMobile: function () { return false; },
        isAvailable: function () { return false; }
      };

      // Register the page-scoped dsModals + dsSolanaModal stores. Named (not an
      // inline alpine:init callback) so the dual-guard at the end can invoke it
      // directly on a Turbo visit, when alpine:init will not fire again.
      function registerDsModals() {
        if (Alpine.store('dsModals')) return;

        // Enter/exit animation registry — keys map to a CSS class (engine-
        // motion.css) plus its duration in ms. Open a modal with
        // { enterAnim: 'shake' } / { exitAnim: 'slide' } to pick one; omitted
        // uses 'pop' (the spring bounce). The directional swap()/advance()
        // slide uses the modal-card-swap-* classes regardless of these keys.
        var CLOSE_ANIM_MS = 220;
        var SWAP_IN_MS    = 220;
        var Anim = {
          enter: {
            pop:   { cls: 'modal-card-mount',    ms: 320 },
            shake: { cls: 'modal-card-shake-in', ms: 600 },
            slide: { cls: 'modal-card-swap-in',  ms: 220 }
          },
          exit: {
            pop:   { cls: 'modal-card-unmount',  ms: 220 },
            slide: { cls: 'modal-card-swap-out', ms: 220 }
          }
        };
        function modalAnim(channel, key) {
          var table = Anim[channel] || {};
          return table[key] || table.pop;
        }

        Alpine.store('dsModals', {
          stack: [],
          current: function () { return this.stack.length ? this.stack[this.stack.length - 1] : null; },
          isOpen: function (id) {
            for (var i = 0; i < this.stack.length; i++) { if (this.stack[i].id === id) return true; }
            return false;
          },
          // open(id, props, opts) — opts.replace swaps the top entry with a
          // directional slide (forward = exit right / enter left); otherwise
          // push (stacking — closing reveals the entry underneath).
          open: function (id, props, opts) {
            props = props || {}; opts = opts || {};
            var self = this;
            if (opts.replace && this.stack.length > 0) {
              var current = this.current();
              if (current && !current._closing) {
                var dir = (opts.direction === 'back') ? 'back' : 'forward';
                current._swapDir = dir;
                current._swappingOut = true;
                current._closing = true;
                setTimeout(function () {
                  var idx = self.stack.indexOf(current);
                  var newEntry = { id: id, props: props, _swappingIn: true, _swapDir: dir };
                  if (idx >= 0) { self.stack[idx] = newEntry; } else { self.stack.push(newEntry); }
                  self._sync();
                  setTimeout(function () {
                    newEntry._swappingIn = false; newEntry._swapDir = null; newEntry._settled = true;
                  }, SWAP_IN_MS);
                }, CLOSE_ANIM_MS);
                return;
              }
              this.stack[this.stack.length - 1] = { id: id, props: props };
            } else {
              this.stack.push({ id: id, props: props });
            }
            this._sync();
          },
          // swap(id, props, opts) ≡ open with { replace: true }.
          swap: function (id, props, opts) {
            return this.open(id, props, Object.assign({ replace: true }, opts || {}));
          },
          // advance(patch, opts) — in-flow step change: same directional slide as
          // swap() but WITHOUT replacing the stack entry, so the modal's outer
          // x-data scope survives (the auth step machine relies on this).
          advance: function (propsPatch, opts) {
            opts = opts || {};
            var cur = this.current();
            if (!cur || cur._closing || cur._swappingOut) return;
            var self = this;
            cur._swapDir = (opts.direction === 'back') ? 'back' : 'forward';
            cur._swappingOut = true;
            setTimeout(function () {
              if (self.stack.indexOf(cur) < 0) return;
              if (propsPatch) Object.assign(cur.props, propsPatch);
              cur._swappingOut = false;
              cur._swappingIn = true;
              setTimeout(function () {
                cur._swappingIn = false; cur._swapDir = null; cur._settled = true;
              }, SWAP_IN_MS);
            }, CLOSE_ANIM_MS);
          },
          close: function () {
            var self = this;
            var entry = this.current();
            if (!entry || entry._closing) return;
            entry._closing = true;
            setTimeout(function () {
              var idx = self.stack.indexOf(entry);
              if (idx >= 0) { self.stack.splice(idx, 1); self._sync(); }
            }, modalAnim('exit', entry.props && entry.props.exitAnim).ms);
          },
          closeAll: function () { this.stack = []; this._sync(); },
          cardClasses: function () {
            var c = this.current();
            if (!c) return {};
            var o = {};
            if (!c._settled && !c._swappingIn && !c._swappingOut && !c._closing) {
              o[modalAnim('enter', c.props && c.props.enterAnim).cls] = true;
            }
            if (c._closing && !c._swappingOut) {
              o[modalAnim('exit', c.props && c.props.exitAnim).cls] = true;
            }
            o['modal-card-swap-in']       = !!(c._swappingIn  && c._swapDir !== 'back');
            o['modal-card-swap-out']      = !!(c._swappingOut && c._swapDir !== 'back');
            o['modal-card-swap-in-back']  = !!(c._swappingIn  && c._swapDir === 'back');
            o['modal-card-swap-out-back'] = !!(c._swappingOut && c._swapDir === 'back');
            return o;
          },
          _sync: function () {
            if (this.stack.length) { document.body.classList.add('modal-open'); }
            else { document.body.classList.remove('modal-open'); }
          }
        });

        // dsSolanaModal — stateless proxy over dsModals for the on-chain-tx
        // modal. Reads the current 'onchain-tx' entry's props so the partial's
        // $store.dsSolanaModal.{state,title,txSignature,...} reads stay stable.
        Alpine.store('dsSolanaModal', {
          _cur: function () { var c = Alpine.store('dsModals').current(); return (c && c.id === 'onchain-tx') ? c : null; },
          _read: function (k, fb) { var c = this._cur(); return c ? (c.props[k] !== undefined ? c.props[k] : fb) : fb; },
          close: function () { if (this._cur()) Alpine.store('dsModals').close(); },
          get state()           { return this._read('state', null); },
          get title()           { return this._read('title', ''); },
          get message()         { return this._read('message', ''); },
          get txSignature()     { return this._read('txSignature', null); },
          get errorMessage()    { return this._read('errorMessage', ''); },
          get successTitle()    { return this._read('successTitle', ''); },
          get successSubtitle() { return this._read('successSubtitle', ''); },
          get ctaLabel()        { return this._read('ctaLabel', ''); },
          get ctaHref()         { return this._read('ctaHref', ''); }
        });
      }

      // Alpine's deferred CDN <script> fires alpine:init exactly ONCE, on the
      // first full-document load. Turbo Drive advance visits swap the document
      // body without reloading that head script, so alpine:init never fires
      // again — and
      // because this dsModals registration lives ONLY in the /admin/style body,
      // it was absent during that one alpine:init. Registering here on the
      // Turbo-visit path (Alpine already started) keeps $store.dsModals defined,
      // so the specimen cards' @click / :style / <template x-if> don't throw.
      // Mirrors studio/modals/_image_upload's cropPhotoModal guard.
      if (window.Alpine) { registerDsModals(); }
      else { document.addEventListener('alpine:init', registerDsModals); }
    })();
  </script>

  <%# The minimum-visible-duration convention (window.StudioModals.holdAtLeast +
      MIN_LOAD_MS) — the SAME single definition the shared modal host renders, so
      the demo load modals here (payment/entry processing, on-chain tx, saving)
      honor resolveAt = max(min_duration, actual) and auto-resolve after
      min_duration in demo mode. A consumer app already has it via the host. %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/load_convention" %>

  <%# Cropper.js + the cropPhotoModal factory — makes the Profile crop / upload
      modals openable on this page (loads cropper.js via <script defer> and
      defines the factory inline; no importmap change). %>
  <%= render "studio/cropper_assets" %>

  <%# ageVerifyModal factory — rendered here at page level (never inside the
      overlay template, where a cloned script would not run) so the age-gate
      specimen opens live. A consumer app renders this in its layout the same way. %>
  <%= render "studio/age_verify_assets" %>

  <%# levelingActionModal factory — page level (never inside the overlay template,
      where a cloned script would not run) so the change-username + join-newsletter
      specimens open live. A consumer app renders this in its layout the same way. %>
  <%= render "studio/leveling_activity_assets" %>

  <%# ---- The overlay: one backdrop + card; every specimen's real content is a
      single-root <template x-if> gated on the current modal id. Faithful to the
      shared host — backdrop fade, scroll lock, escape + click-self dismissal
      gated on props.dismissible (never @click.outside, so a hold modal can't
      close itself on the button release). %>
  <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current()">
    <div class="fixed inset-0 z-[120] flex items-center justify-center p-4 modal-backdrop-mount"
         :class="$store.dsModals.current()?._closing && 'modal-backdrop-unmount'"
         style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6)"
         role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
         @keydown.escape.window="$store.dsModals.current() && $store.dsModals.current().props.dismissible !== false && $store.dsModals.close()"
         @click.self="$store.dsModals.current() && $store.dsModals.current().props.dismissible !== false && $store.dsModals.close()">
      <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-subtle shadow-2xl p-6 max-w-sm w-full"
           :class="$store.dsModals.cardClasses()">

        <%# --- Auth suite --- %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'auth'">
          <div><%= render "style/modals/auth" %></div>
        </template>

        <%# --- Eligibility + entry --- %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'age-verify'">
          <div><%= render "style/modals/age_verify" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'entry-tokens'">
          <div><%= render "style/modals/entry_tokens" %></div>
        </template>

        <%# --- Profile (real engine partials, opened on dsModals) --- %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'crop-photo'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/crop_photo", store: "dsModals" %></div>
        </template>
        <%# saving — the demo passes resolve_expr so the spinner self-terminates
            after min_duration (a real app's Turbo submit drives + closes it). %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'saving'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/saving", store: "dsModals",
                    resolve_expr: "$store.dsModals.close()" %></div>
        </template>

        <%# --- Web3 --- %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'wallet-connect'">
          <div><%= render "style/modals/wallet_connect" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'onchain-tx'">
          <div><%= render "style/modals/onchain_tx" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'wallet-deposit'">
          <div><%= render "style/modals/wallet_deposit" %></div>
        </template>
        <%# entry-confirmed — the engine celebration composed via _success_card's
            yield. One registration serves the generic (web3) + seeds (leveling)
            specimens; the seeds bar self-gates on Studio.feature?(:leveling). %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'entry-confirmed'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/entry_confirmed",
                    modal_store: "dsModals",
                    cta_label: "Contest Lobby ⚔️",
                    free_entry_label: "Free Entry Earned 🎟️" %></div>
        </template>

        <%# --- System and status (reusable card blocks) --- %>
        <%# ds-processing demos the min-duration convention on the canonical block:
            resolve_expr auto-swaps to the success card after min_duration. %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'ds-processing'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/processing_card",
                    title: "Confirming entry", message: "Talking to the server…",
                    resolve_expr: "$store.dsModals.swap('ds-success')" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'ds-success'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/success_card",
                    title: "Entry confirmed", message: "You're in — good luck!",
                    icon_color: "success", cta_label: "Continue", cta_event: "ds-modal-close" do %><% end %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'ds-error'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/error_card",
                    title: "Couldn't connect", icon_emoji: "⚠️",
                    message: "Something went wrong. Give it another try.",
                    cta_label: "Try again", cta_event: "ds-modal-close",
                    secondary_label: "Dismiss", secondary_event: "ds-modal-close" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'ds-countdown'">
          <div x-data="{ n: 5, t: 5, timer: null }"
               x-init="timer = setInterval(() => { if (n > 0) { n--; } else { clearInterval(timer); } }, 1000)">
            <div class="text-center mb-4">
              <p class="text-heading font-bold text-lg mb-1">Heading to the lobby</p>
              <p class="text-secondary text-xs">Sit tight — this happens automatically.</p>
            </div>
            <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/progress_countdown", current_key: "n", total_key: "t" %>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm w-full mt-4"
                    @click="$store.dsModals.close()">Cancel</button>
          </div>
        </template>

        <%# --- Templates (copy-from archetypes) --- %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'template-wizard'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/templates/wizard", modal_store: "dsModals" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'template-form'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/templates/form", modal_store: "dsModals" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'template-action'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/templates/action", modal_store: "dsModals" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'template-status'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/templates/status", modal_store: "dsModals" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'template-success'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/templates/success", modal_store: "dsModals" %></div>
        </template>

        <%# --- Rewards / leveling --- %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'levelup'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/success_card",
                    title: "Level 10!", message: "You leveled up.", icon_emoji: "🎉",
                    large_title: true, cta_label: "Nice", cta_event: "ds-modal-close" do %>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="sheen sheen--loop studio-glow studio-glow--pulse inline-flex h-14 w-14 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-white text-lg font-extrabold"
                    style="background: var(--color-cta); --studio-glow-color: var(--color-success)">10</span>
            </div>
          <% end %></div>
        </template>
        <%# free-entry-earned — the standalone level-up reward modal (:leveling). %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'free-entry-earned'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/free_entry_earned",
                    modal_store: "dsModals",
                    subtitle: "You leveled up! A Free Entry lands in your account soon. Keep leveling for more." %></div>
        </template>

        <%# --- Profile Leveling: change username + join newsletter --- %>
        <%# ONE id per activity — opened at the form OR (with props.celebrate) at the
            "updated" state, exactly like the Auth cards open a given step. The
            primitive reads props.leveling at RUNTIME, so each card's own Leveling
            toggle flips TM (the seeds celebration) <-> MS (plain confirmation) at
            open — no more `-plain` twins, and no "Quest N of N" counter. All
            demo:true (the save resolves locally); the on-chain-accurate copy is an
            app-authored description (the engine default stays neutral). The two
            activities walk in sequence via the celebration's "Next Quest"
            (Username -> Newsletter -> close). %>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'change-username'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/change_username",
                    modal_store: "dsModals", demo: true, leveling: true,
                    current_username: "turfmonster",
                    submit_url: "#demo-change-username",
                    description: "Your username is stored on-chain. Changes are saved via your managed wallet.",
                    cta_label: "Save", saved_label: "Saved",
                    demo_seeds_earned: 25, demo_seeds_total: 25,
                    free_entry_label: "Free Entry Token 🎟️",
                    confirm_subtitle: "Your username has been updated.",
                    next_label: "Next Quest",
                    next_open: "$store.dsModals.swap('join-newsletter', { demo: true, leveling: true })" %></div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="$store.dsModals.current().id === 'join-newsletter'">
          <div><%= render "studio/modals/blocks/leveling_activity",
                    modal_store: "dsModals", demo: true, leveling: true,
                    submit_url: "#demo-newsletter",
                    title: "Join the Newsletter",
                    description: "Sports news and contest updates — and 25 seeds for joining.",
                    input: false,
                    consent_label: "Email me sports news and contest updates.",
                    cta_label: "Subscribe", saved_label: "Subscribed", saving_label: "Subscribing…",
                    icon_emoji: "🌱",
                    celebrate_title: "Subscribed!",
                    celebrate_subtitle: "You're on the list. We'll keep the sports news and contest updates coming.",
                    demo_seeds_earned: 25, demo_seeds_total: 100,
                    free_entry_label: "Free Entry Token 🎟️",
                    confirm_subtitle: "You're on the list.",
                    next_label: "Next Quest",
                    next_open: "$store.dsModals.close()" %></div>
        </template>

      </div>
    </div>
  </template>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 1. AUTH suite %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Auth</h3>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The sign-in step machine
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">style/modals/_auth</code>) — one modal,
        internal steps <code class="font-mono text-2xs">credentials &rarr;
        magic-link-sent &rarr; magic-link-resent</code>. Toggle the methods below a
        card, then open it to watch them gate the modal. The live card
        <strong>glows</strong>, and the glow follows the step machine as you advance.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%# Sign in — method toggles + the credentials-step glow. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Sign in",
            reference: %(the Auth "Sign in" modal (studio-engine style/modals/_auth, step 'credentials') — open with $store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'credentials', picksRequired: 6 }); toggle methods via props.methods { magicLink, google, wallet } + props.terms),
            card_data: "opts: { magicLink: #{ml_default}, google: #{g_default}, wallet: #{w_default}, terms: true }",
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'credentials', picksRequired: 6, methods: { magicLink: opts.magicLink, google: opts.google, wallet: opts.wallet }, terms: opts.terms })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("auth", step: "credentials"),
            toggles: [
              { model: "opts.magicLink", label: "Magic Link" },
              { model: "opts.google",    label: "Google" },
              { model: "opts.wallet",    label: "Solana Wallet" },
              { model: "opts.terms",     label: "Terms" }
            ] } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2 text-center">
          <span class="block h-2 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity: .5"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Magic link sent",
            reference: %(the Auth "Magic link sent" step (style/modals/_auth, step 'magic-link-sent') — open with $store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'magic-link-sent', sentEmail: 'you@example.com' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'magic-link-sent', sentEmail: 'you@example.com' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("auth", step: "magic-link-sent") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">📬</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# NEW — the magic-link-resent step (the resend confirmation slide). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Magic link resent",
            reference: %(the Auth "Magic link resent" step (style/modals/_auth, step 'magic-link-resent') — open with $store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'magic-link-resent', sentEmail: 'you@example.com' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'magic-link-resent', sentEmail: 'you@example.com' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("auth", step: "magic-link-resent") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-primary)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Redirect (drain)",
            reference: %(the Auth "Redirect" step (style/modals/_auth, step 'redirect', drain CTA) — open with $store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'redirect', icon: '📍', title: 'One more step', message: 'Taking you there.', url: null })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('auth', { step: 'redirect', icon: '📍', title: 'One more step', message: 'Taking you there.', url: null })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("auth", step: "redirect") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">📍</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 2. PROFILE — crop / upload, live via cropper_assets %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Profile</h3>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The avatar / photo modals ship from the engine
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/_crop_photo</code>,
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/_image_upload</code>) and
        open live here — <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/cropper_assets</code>
        is rendered above, so cropper.js loads and the modals mount on this page's
        host.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%# Image upload FIRST — the empty picker (crop-photo opened with no imageUrl).
          cropReady: false is the defined starting sub-state; the crop factory
          flips it true once an image is picked, moving the glow to Crop photo. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Image upload",
            reference: %(the Profile "Image upload" modal (studio-engine studio/modals/_crop_photo as the empty picker) — open with $store.dsModals.open('crop-photo', {})),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('crop-photo', { cropReady: false })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("crop-photo", crop: :picker) } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-20 h-20 rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed flex items-center justify-center" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)">
            <span class="text-2xl leading-none">⬆️</span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Crop photo SECOND — the cropper mounted on a chosen image. cropReady:
          true glows this card immediately on a direct open (the factory also sets
          it when the cropper mounts). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Crop photo",
            reference: %(the Profile "Crop photo" modal (studio/modals/_crop_photo + studio/_cropper_assets) — open with $store.dsModals.open('crop-photo', { imageUrl: '/icon.png', aspectRatio: 1 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('crop-photo', { imageUrl: '/icon.png', aspectRatio: 1, cropReady: true })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("crop-photo", crop: :crop) } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-20 h-20 rounded-lg border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="border-color: var(--color-cta)">
            <span class="text-muted text-2xs">Crop area</span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Saving card",
            reference: %(the Profile "Saving" card (studio/modals/_saving loading state) — open with $store.dsModals.open('saving', { title: 'Saving…' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('saving', { title: 'Saving…' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("saving") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-8 h-8 rounded-full border-4 animate-spin" style="border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-cta) 30%, transparent); border-top-color: var(--color-cta)"></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 3. PROFILE LEVELING — change username + join newsletter (per-card toggles) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# Each specimen card carries its OWN Leveling toggle (like the Auth "Sign in"
      card's method checkboxes) — the card's opts.leveling flows into its open() as
      props.leveling, so the card opens at the TM shape (checked, the default) or the
      MS shape (unchecked). Independent per card: preview Change Username leveling-on
      beside Great Username leveling-off. ONE primitive, ONE id per activity, no
      "Quest N of N" counter — the with/without fork is gone. The two "updated"
      cards open the same modal id straight at the celebrate state (props.celebrate),
      exactly like the Auth cards open a given step. %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Profile Leveling</h3>
        <% if leveling_on %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-success); border-color: var(--color-success)">leveling on</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-warning); border-color: var(--color-warning)">leveling off</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The profile leveling flow, ported from Turf Monster as ONE primitive
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/blocks/_leveling_activity</code>,
        with <code class="font-mono text-2xs">_change_username</code> as its username
        specialization). Walk all four states — <strong>Change Username &rarr; Great
        Username</strong>, then <strong>Join the Newsletter &rarr; Subscribed!</strong>
        — each "updated" card opens its modal straight at the success state, just like
        the Auth cards open a given step. Each card carries its <strong>own Leveling
        toggle</strong> (like the Auth card's method checkboxes): <strong>checked</strong>
        is the Turf Monster shape (the seeds bar + Free Entry Token progress),
        <strong>unchecked</strong> is the McRitchie Studio shape (plain input + Save,
        then a simple confirmation). Flip a card's toggle, then open it — so you can
        preview Change Username leveling-on beside Great Username leveling-off. Same
        modal id either way — the primitive reads
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">leveling</code> at runtime, so there is no
        with/without fork and <strong>no "Quest N of N" counter</strong>. The save is an
        <strong>app-supplied callback</strong>
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">submit_url</code> + an opaque
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">finalize_hook</code> for a wallet step) —
        <strong>no wallet, signing, or on-chain write lives in the engine</strong>.
        (These demos resolve locally.)
      </p>
    </div>
    <%# The walk, left to right: Change Username -> Great Username -> Join Newsletter
        -> Subscribed. The two "updated" cards open the same id at props.celebrate. %>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <%# 1. Change Username — the input (form) state. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Change Username",
            reference: %(the Profile Leveling "Change Username" activity (studio-engine studio/modals/blocks/_change_username) — the input state. Reads leveling at runtime; the on-chain save is an app-supplied callback (submit_url + an opaque finalize_hook), the engine is UI only. Open with $store.dsModals.open('change-username', { demo: true, leveling: true })),
            card_data: "opts: { leveling: true }",
            toggles:   [{ model: "opts.leveling", label: "Leveling" }],
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('change-username', { demo: true, leveling: opts.leveling })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("change-username", celebrate: false) } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-16 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 2. Great Username — the updated (celebrate) state, opened directly. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Great Username",
            reference: %(the Profile Leveling "Great Username" updated state (studio/modals/blocks/_change_username opened at props.celebrate) — leveling ON shows the seeds celebration (plus 25, Free Entry Token) + Next Quest; leveling OFF shows the plain "Saved" confirmation. Toggle this card's Leveling checkbox to switch, then open. Open with $store.dsModals.open('change-username', { demo: true, leveling: true, celebrate: true, seedsEarned: 25, seedsTotal: 25 })),
            card_data: "opts: { leveling: true }",
            toggles:   [{ model: "opts.leveling", label: "Leveling" }],
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('change-username', { demo: true, leveling: opts.leveling, celebrate: true, seedsEarned: 25, seedsTotal: 25 })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("change-username", celebrate: true) } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">🌱</div>
          <div x-show="opts.leveling" class="flex gap-1">
            <span class="flex-1 h-2 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.5"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity:.12"></span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 3. Join the Newsletter — the input state (consent checkbox + Subscribe). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Join Newsletter",
            reference: %(the Profile Leveling "Join the Newsletter" activity (studio-engine studio/modals/blocks/_leveling_activity) — the input state: a consent checkbox + Subscribe. Reads leveling at runtime. Open with $store.dsModals.open('join-newsletter', { demo: true, leveling: true })),
            card_data: "opts: { leveling: true }",
            toggles:   [{ model: "opts.leveling", label: "Leveling" }],
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('join-newsletter', { demo: true, leveling: opts.leveling })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("join-newsletter", celebrate: false) } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2">
          <span class="text-lg leading-none">📬</span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 4. Subscribed! — the updated (celebrate) state, opened directly. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Subscribed!",
            reference: %(the Profile Leveling "Subscribed!" updated state (studio/modals/blocks/_leveling_activity opened at props.celebrate) — leveling ON shows the seeds celebration (Free Entry Token) + Next Quest; leveling OFF shows the plain "Subscribed" confirmation. Toggle this card's Leveling checkbox to switch, then open. Open with $store.dsModals.open('join-newsletter', { demo: true, leveling: true, celebrate: true, seedsEarned: 25, seedsTotal: 100 })),
            card_data: "opts: { leveling: true }",
            toggles:   [{ model: "opts.leveling", label: "Leveling" }],
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('join-newsletter', { demo: true, leveling: opts.leveling, celebrate: true, seedsEarned: 25, seedsTotal: 100 })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("join-newsletter", celebrate: true) } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-success)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div x-show="opts.leveling" class="flex gap-1">
            <span class="flex-1 h-2 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.6"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.3"></span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 2. WEB3 CONTEST — the walked wallet -> on-chain flow (glow follows it). %>
  <%# Gated by :web3; off = disabled-but-present-yet-openable. %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Web3 Contest</h3>
        <% if web3_on %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-success); border-color: var(--color-success)">enabled on this app</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-warning); border-color: var(--color-warning)">disabled on this app</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The wallet + on-chain modals, ported into the engine and gated by
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">Studio.feature?(:web3)</code>. Web3 is
        <strong><%= web3_on ? "on" : "off" %></strong> here, so these render
        <%= web3_on ? "live." : "greyed and badged — but STILL openable as a preview." %>
        The first three cards are a <strong>walked flow</strong> &mdash;
        <strong>Connect Wallet &rarr; Processing on-chain transaction &rarr; On-chain
        success</strong> &mdash; and the live card <strong>glows</strong>, following the
        flow as it advances (open Connect Wallet and pick a wallet to watch it walk).
        The <strong>Processing</strong> card is a load modal: its
        <strong>success/error toggle</strong> chooses whether it resolves to success
        or the error state, after the <strong>minimum-visible duration</strong>
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/_load_convention</code>). The
        Connect-wallet picker ships its <strong>Phantom / Solflare / Backpack brand
        marks inline from the engine</strong>
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/blocks/_wallet_brand_sprite</code>),
        so every app inherits them with no per-app icon files.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%# 1. Connect wallet — the walk's entry; picking a wallet swaps to Processing. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Connect wallet",
            reference: %(the Web3 Contest "Connect wallet" picker (studio-engine style/modals/_wallet_connect) — the walk's entry: picking a wallet runs a brief connecting state then swaps to the on-chain Processing modal. Open with $store.dsModals.open('wallet-connect')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('wallet-connect')",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("wallet-connect"),
            disabled: !web3_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 2. Processing — the load modal; the success/error toggle picks the resolution. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Processing on-chain tx",
            reference: %(the Web3 Contest "Processing" on-chain load modal (style/modals/_onchain_tx via $store.dsSolanaModal) — holds the spinner at least MIN_LOAD_MS, then auto-resolves to success (or the error state when the toggle is set). Open with $store.dsModals.open('onchain-tx', { state: 'processing', demoResolve: true, demoError: false })),
            card_data: "opts: { demoError: false }",
            toggles:   [{ model: "opts.demoError", label: "Resolve to error" }],
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('onchain-tx', { state: 'processing', title: 'Confirming on-chain', message: 'Waiting for the wallet signature…', demoResolve: true, demoError: opts.demoError })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("onchain-tx", state: "processing"),
            disabled: !web3_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="loading-dots mx-auto"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 3. On-chain success — the resolved success end-state (the walk's finish). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "On-chain success",
            reference: %(the Web3 Contest "On-chain success" state (style/modals/_onchain_tx + studio/modals/blocks/_onchain_success) — the resolved success card the walk lands on. Open with $store.dsModals.open('onchain-tx', { state: 'success', txSignature: '…', successTitle: 'Mint complete' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('onchain-tx', { state: 'success', txSignature: '5xTrDemoSignature1234567890', successTitle: 'Mint complete', successSubtitle: 'Your on-chain action confirmed.', ctaLabel: 'View wallet', ctaHref: null })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("onchain-tx", state: "success"),
            disabled: !web3_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-success)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# On-chain error — the resolved error end-state (the toggle's other branch). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "On-chain error",
            reference: %(the Web3 Contest "On-chain error" state (style/modals/_onchain_tx) — the resolved error card the Processing toggle resolves to. Open with $store.dsModals.open('onchain-tx', { state: 'error', title: "Couldn't confirm", errorMessage: 'The transaction was rejected. Give it another try.' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('onchain-tx', { state: 'error', title: 'Could not confirm', errorMessage: 'The transaction was rejected. Give it another try.' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("onchain-tx", state: "error"),
            disabled: !web3_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">⚠️</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Wallet deposit — standalone top-up card (not part of the walk). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Wallet deposit",
            reference: %(the Web3 Contest "Wallet deposit" top-up card (style/modals/_wallet_deposit) — open with $store.dsModals.open('wallet-deposit', { neededCents: 500, usdcCents: 120, usdtCents: 0, address: 'Fo1L5…' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('wallet-deposit', { neededCents: 500, usdcCents: 120, usdtCents: 0, address: 'Fo1L5demoWALLETaddr9xQ2' })",
            disabled: !web3_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Entry confirmed — the GENERIC web3 celebration (tx link + heading + drain
          CTA). seedsEarned: 0 so no seeds bar even where leveling is on: this card
          demos the clean success a web3-only app gets. The seeds variant lives in
          Rewards below (gated by :leveling). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry confirmed",
            reference: %(the Web3 Contest "Entry confirmed" celebration (studio/modals/blocks/_entry_confirmed, composed via _success_card's yield — branded tx link + heading + drain CTA; the seeds bar is gated off by :leveling and stays hidden here) — open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-confirmed', { txSignature: '…', lobbyUrl: null, seedsEarned: 0 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-confirmed', { txSignature: '5xTrDemoSignature1234567890abcXYZ', lobbyUrl: null, seedsEarned: 0, seedsTotal: 40 })",
            disabled: !web3_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-primary)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-14 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 3. CONTEST ENTRY & ELIGIBILITY — moved directly under Web3 Contest. The %>
  <%# walked entry flow (glow follows), plus the honest web2/web3 map. %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Contest entry &amp; eligibility</h3>
        <% if age_gate_on %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-success); border-color: var(--color-success)">age gate on</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-warning); border-color: var(--color-warning)">age gate off</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The pre-entry gate and the full entry flow. The <strong>age gate</strong>
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/blocks/_age_verify</code>) is an
        engine primitive gated by
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">Studio.feature?(:age_gate)</code> &mdash; a DOB
        modal whose minimum age, jurisdiction label, endpoint, and legal copy are all
        <strong>app-supplied</strong> (the engine hardcodes no policy). The entry flow is
        a <strong>walked sequence</strong> &mdash; <strong>Entry tokens &rarr; Payment
        processing &rarr; Entry Tokens Minted &rarr; Contest enter processing &rarr;
        Contest entered</strong> &mdash; and the live card <strong>glows</strong>,
        following the step machine (the two load steps honor the same min-duration
        convention as Web3 Contest above).
      </p>
      <%# The web2/web3 finding — a real divergence, stated honestly, not invented. %>
      <div class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface p-3 text-xs text-secondary leading-snug">
        <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-1">Web2 vs web3 — the honest map</p>
        <p class="mb-1">
          The two funding paths <strong>diverge at the front-end and the entry-submit
          endpoint, then converge</strong>. <strong>Web2</strong> (card / Stripe /
          Coinflow / PayPal) mints one prepaid entry token per credit on-chain after
          payment clears, then <strong>consumes</strong> one token to enter.
          <strong>Web3</strong> (wallet / USDC on-chain) funds USDC directly and
          <strong>mints no token</strong> &mdash; the mint&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;consume prelude
          is web2-only.
        </p>
        <p>
          Both create the <strong>same on-chain Entry PDA</strong> and resolve to the
          <strong>same “Entry Confirmed” card</strong>. The walk below demos the web2
          path end-to-end; web3 skips the mint and joins at
          <strong>enter&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;entered</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%# Age gate — engine primitive, gated on :age_gate (disabled-but-present). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Age gate (DOB)",
            reference: %(the "Age gate" DOB modal (studio-engine studio/modals/blocks/_age_verify) — an engine primitive; the app supplies min_age / state / submit_url / fine_print and the engine hardcodes no legal policy. In this demo, Confirm & Continue advances to the Entry tokens purchase (page-level dsModals wiring on the primitive's 'age-verified' hook; the primitive's real submit posts to submit_url). Open with $store.dsModals.open('age-verify')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('age-verify')",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("age-verify"),
            disabled: !age_gate_on, openable: true, disabled_label: "age gate off" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2 text-center">
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-1">
            <span class="h-6 rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
            <span class="h-6 rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
            <span class="h-6 rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 1. Entry tokens — the picker (walk's entry). Picking a pack advances. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry tokens",
            reference: %(the "Entry tokens" picker (app-specific — documented composing studio/modals/blocks chrome). The packs, pricing, rails, and on-chain mint stay app-owned. Picking a pack walks Payment processing -> Minted -> enter -> entered. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'picker' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'picker' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "picker", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-primary)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 2. Payment processing — the mint-at-purchase load step (web2). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Payment processing",
            reference: %(the "Payment processing" step (entry-tokens step 'confirming') — "Confirming your purchase…" over "Payment cleared — a server job mints one prepaid entry credit per token on-chain." A load modal; honors the min-duration convention then auto-advances to Entry Tokens Minted. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'confirming', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'confirming', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "confirming", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="loading-dots mx-auto"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 3. Entry Tokens Minted — ready to consume at entry (hold to confirm). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry Tokens Minted",
            reference: %(the "Entry Tokens Minted" step (entry-tokens step 'minted') — "You now have N available." Holding to confirm consumes one token on-chain to create the contest entry (advances to Contest enter processing). Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'minted', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'minted', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "minted", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 15%, transparent)">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold" style="color: var(--color-primary)">3</span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 4. Contest enter processing — the on-chain consume load step. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Contest enter processing",
            reference: %(the "Contest enter processing" step (entry-tokens step 'entering') — "Confirming your entry…" over "Consuming one token on-chain to create your contest entry." A load modal; honors the min-duration convention then auto-advances to Contest entered. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entering' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entering' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "entering", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="loading-dots mx-auto"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 5. Contest entered — the shared Entry Confirmed finish (web2 + web3 converge). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Contest entered",
            reference: %(the "Contest entered" success (entry-tokens step 'entered') — "Good Luck / Entry Confirmed" with the branded on-chain tx link and a Contest Lobby CTA. The SAME finish both web2 and web3 entries converge on. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entered', txSignature: '…' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entered', txSignature: '5xTrDemoEntrySignature1234567890abc' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "entered", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-success)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 5. SYSTEM AND STATUS (reusable card blocks) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">System &amp; status</h3>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The reusable card blocks under <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/blocks/</code> &mdash;
        the studio-canonical processing, success, error, and countdown states.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Processing",
            reference: %(the "Processing" card block (studio/modals/blocks/_processing_card) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-processing')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-processing')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 animate-spin" style="border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-cta) 30%, transparent); border-top-color: var(--color-cta)"></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Success",
            reference: %(the "Success" card block (studio/modals/blocks/_success_card, entry-confirmed style) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-success')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-success')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-success)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Error / retry",
            reference: %(the "Error" card block (studio/modals/blocks/_error_card) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-error')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-error')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">⚠️</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-20 mx-auto rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Countdown",
            reference: %(the "Countdown" progress block (studio/modals/blocks/_progress_countdown) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-countdown')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-countdown')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <div class="w-full rounded-full overflow-hidden" style="height: 6px; background: rgba(128,128,128,0.2)">
            <div style="height: 100%; width: 60%; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--color-cta)"></div>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 6. TEMPLATES (copy-from archetypes) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Templates</h3>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        Reusable archetypes under <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/templates/</code> &mdash;
        the copy-from reference cards for a new modal (wizard, form, action,
        status, success).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
      <% [
           ["template-wizard",  "Wizard",  "🧭", "studio/modals/templates/_wizard"],
           ["template-form",    "Form",    "📝", "studio/modals/templates/_form"],
           ["template-action",  "Action",  "❓", "studio/modals/templates/_action"],
           ["template-status",  "Status",  "⏳", "studio/modals/templates/_status"],
           ["template-success", "Success", "✅", "studio/modals/templates/_success"]
         ].each do |id, label, glyph, partial| %>
        <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
              label:     label,
              reference: %(the "#{label}" modal template (#{partial}) — open with $store.dsModals.open('#{id}')),
              open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('#{id}')" } do %>
          <div class="pointer-events-none w-32 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
            <div class="text-2xl leading-none"><%= glyph %></div>
            <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
            <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity: .6"></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 7. REWARDS / leveling (gated by Studio.feature?(:leveling)) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Rewards</h3>
        <% if leveling_on %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-success); border-color: var(--color-success)">enabled on this app</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-warning); border-color: var(--color-warning)">disabled on this app</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The seeds bar + level-up celebrations, gated by
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">Studio.feature?(:leveling)</code> — an
        app-level setting <strong>independent of :web3</strong> (some apps have
        Solana but no leveling). Leveling is <strong><%= leveling_on ? "on" : "off" %></strong>
        here, so these render
        <%= leveling_on ? "live." : "greyed and badged — but STILL openable as a preview." %>
        The seed counts, level, and free entry are <strong>app-supplied props</strong>
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">seedsEarned</code>,
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">seedsTotal</code>, …) — the engine renders
        the bar, the app feeds the numbers.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Level up",
            reference: %(the Rewards "Level up" celebration (studio/modals/blocks/_success_card with the sheen + studio-glow badge) — open with $store.dsModals.open('levelup')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('levelup')",
            disabled: !leveling_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">🎉</div>
          <span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-white text-sm font-extrabold" style="background: var(--color-cta)">10</span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Entry + seeds — the SAME _entry_confirmed card, now with seedsEarned
          crossing a level so the :leveling seeds bar mounts in the _success_card
          yield and plays the 4-phase level-up (fill → pop → drain → refill), then
          swaps to the Free Entry Earned reward line. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry + seeds level-up",
            reference: %(the Rewards "Entry + seeds" celebration (studio/modals/blocks/_entry_confirmed — the :leveling seeds bar + Free Entry Earned reward injected into _success_card's yield) — open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-confirmed', { txSignature: '…', lobbyUrl: null, seedsEarned: 30, seedsTotal: 100 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-confirmed', { txSignature: '5xTrDemoSignature1234567890abcXYZ', lobbyUrl: null, seedsEarned: 30, seedsTotal: 100 })",
            disabled: !leveling_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-primary)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-1">
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.6"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.25"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity:.12"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity:.12"></span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Free Entry Earned — the standalone level-up reward modal (:leveling). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Free Entry Earned",
            reference: %(the Rewards "Free Entry Earned" level-up modal (studio/modals/blocks/_free_entry_earned) — open with $store.dsModals.open('free-entry-earned', { level: 3 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('free-entry-earned', { level: 3 })",
            disabled: !leveling_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
